From: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: mt7996: avoid scheduling reset work during probe

Probe errors are unwound by the caller. Do not queue reset work until
initialization has completed, so recovery cannot race with probe cleanup.

Signed-off-by: Iscle <albertiscle9@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -229,7 +229,8 @@
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n",
 			cmd, seq);
 
-		if (!test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
+		if (dev->recovery.hw_init_done &&
+		    !test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
 			dev->recovery.restart = true;
 			wake_up(&dev->mt76.mcu.wait);
 			queue_work(dev->mt76.wq, &dev->reset_work);
